name: Partner settlement
tagline: "Agreement-aware partner statement settlement - effective-dated terms, a cycle calendar, statement integrity and a per-agreement compare, over a synthetic corpus"
description: "A partner / wholesale settlement content pack (slices S1 to S4 of the plan: References, statement ingestion, the compare, and netting positions with a roll-forward). Four Reference feeds (partners, effective-dated settlement agreements, daily FX rates, public holidays), a partner statement feed (versioned lines with control totals), a finance payment feed (payments, credit and debit notes) and a stand-in re-rated usage feed that implements the contract the re-rating pack will fill. Nine chained sql.template Jobs: a settlement-cycle calendar (statement due, dispute window and payment due dates rolled to business days), the current statement lines (re-sends counted once, the highest version wins), statement integrity findings (control total mismatch, duplicate, restated, unknown partner, unknown agreement), our expected amounts and the partner's billed amounts at one grain in the settlement currency, and the settlement findings (amount mismatch, cut-off difference, FX difference, missing statement, unrated usage, missing FX rate); then every money movement at line level with both currencies and the FX row that converted it, a settlement position per netting group and cycle month (payable, receivable, net, the net in each original currency) and a roll-forward (opening + invoiced - paid + adjustments = closing, one row for every month so a quiet month carries the balance). Per-agreement tolerance, FX and cut-off come from the agreement Reference through the SQL; two Reconciliations (voice, SMS) compare the normalised Datasets at exact tolerance 0 and supply the Break lifecycle and Incidents. One Alert Rule fires once per agreement. It nets inside one currency, reads no dispute, and does not post payments, ledger entries or accruals, and it fetches no market FX rate. Every feed format is synthetic: no real partner statement has been seen. Needs the Standard, Advanced or Preview edition. Runbook: config/runbooks/partner-settlement-runbooks.md."
minEdition: standard
icon: heroicons_outline:arrows-right-left
contents[7]: "7 Pipelines + canonical schemas (4 References, the statement feed, the finance payment feed, the stand-in re-rated usage feed)", "9 chained sql.template Jobs (calendar, current statements, statement integrity, expected, billed, findings, movements, position, roll-forward)", "2 Reconciliations (voice, SMS) with their recon.run Jobs", "1 Alert Rule (one Alert per agreement)", "16 Datasets (7 feeds, 9 Job-written)", "Zero-row schema seeds", "Runbook"
